  "alt": "A long prompt split into its start, middle, and end. The model reliably recalls facts placed at the start, which frames the task, and at the end, which is the runway to the next token. Facts buried in the middle compete for whatever attention is left and often get skipped.",
  "caption": "Models recall facts at the start and the end of a prompt better than facts in the middle. Put the instruction and the data you care about at the start or the end.",
  "embed": "<figure class=\"np-figure\">\n  <a class=\"np-figure-zoom\" href=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-context-windows/lost-in-the-middle.svg\"><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 712px)\" srcset=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-context-windows/lost-in-the-middle.narrow.svg\" width=\"288\" height=\"528\"><img class=\"np-has-narrow\" src=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-context-windows/lost-in-the-middle.svg\" width=\"720\" height=\"544\" alt=\"A long prompt split into its start, middle, and end. The model reliably recalls facts placed at the start, which frames the task, and at the end, which is the runway to the next token. Facts buried in the middle compete for whatever attention is left and often get skipped.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></picture></a>\n  <figcaption>Models recall facts at the start and the end of a prompt better than facts in the middle. Put the instruction and the data you care about at the start or the end.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
